            },
            "output": "<path>/mnt/d/physics-job-hunter/AGENTS.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Physics Job Hunter — Agent Guide\n2: \n3: ## Entrypoints\n4: \n5: - **CLI**: `physics-job-hunter` (needs `pip install -e .` first) or `python3 -m src.main` (works without install)\n6: - **Scheduler**: `nohup python3 -c \"from src.scheduler.daily_run import start; start()\" > /tmp/scheduler.log 2>&1 &` (APScheduler, not OS cron; accepts comma-separated times in `SCHEDULE_TIME`, e.g. `08:00,17:00,22:00,22:30,23:00`)\n7: - **Stop scheduler**: `kill <PID>` (find PID via `ps aux | grep daily_run` or the `echo $!` from the nohup command)\n8: - **Check scheduler logs**: `cat /tmp/scheduler.log`\n9: - No web server or API — fully script-based pipeline.\n10: \n11: ## Pipeline (in order)\n12: \n13: `src/main.py:run_pipeline()`:\n14: 1. **Scrape** — `TESScraper` (works) + `LibyanJobsScraper` (works) + `LinkedInScraper` (placeholder) + `SearchAssociatesScraper` (placeholder) + `SchroleScraper` (placeholder)\n15: 2. **Heuristic pre-filter** — `filter_relevant_jobs()` drops jobs whose title/subject don't match `CORE_KEYWORDS` (physics, maths, science, IGCSE, A-Level, etc.)\n16: 3. **Deduplicate** — skip URLs already in Supabase (falls back to `DedupStore` SQLite if Supabase down)\n17: 4. **Upsert** — `SupabaseClient.upsert_jobs()` into `job_listings` table\n18: 5. **Score** — `LLMScorer` uses a **Weighted Provider Registry** — probes every registered provider at startup via `validate_provider_configs()`, removes dead ones, queries survivors in weight order. Active providers: **Groq** (highest weight, de facto primary) → **NVIDIA** → OpenRouter → OpenCode Zen → Gemini (all three latter are placeholder/429'd). Each provider uses **intra-provider model rotation** with **tenacity exponential backoff** (3 attempts, `wait_random_exponential(multiplier=1, max=60)`). Batch scoring packs **5 jobs per chunk** (`MAX_PER_CHUNK=5`) with a 20s leaky-bucket delay. If all providers fail, falls back to rule-based scoring — **NOTE: `SCORER_PROVIDER` and `SCORER_FALLBACK` env vars are NOT consumed by the scorer**; provider selection is determined by API key presence + `PROVIDER_WEIGHTS`.\n19: 6. **Notify** — Telegram (`src/notify/telegram.py`, runnable directly) + Email (`src/notify/email_sender.py`, Resend or SMTP) for jobs scored ≥ 80\n20: \n21: ## Important gotchas\n22: \n23: - **Python >= 3.12** required\n24: - **`.env` is committed with real API keys** — do NOT modify or commit changes to `.env`; it contains live Supabase and LLM provider credentials\n25: - **`tests/test_gemini_smoke.py`** — smoke test for LLM provider resolution and scoring; run via `python3 tests/test_gemini_smoke.py`\n26: - **`src/extractors/` is empty** — planned but not implemented\n27: - **`LinkedInScraper` is a placeholder** — `scrape()` always returns `[]`\n28: - **`TeacherHorizonsScraper` is bypassed** — removed from `main.py` scrapers list because job detail pages require an activated teacher account; list-view data lacked school name and salary\n29: - **Supabase DNS flaky** — when `httpx.HTTPError` is caught, `SupabaseClient` falls back to `DedupStore` (SQLite at `data/dedup.db`) for all operations: dedup, cache, score, notify. State persists across runs.\n30: - **LibyanJobsScraper** — WordPress theme; each job is `<article.loadmore-item.noo_job>` (not individual row divs). Up to 30 jobs across 3 pages.\n31: - **Cover letter evaluation loop** — `_run_evaluation_loop` has `time.sleep(5)` between provider calls to avoid 429s on free OpenRouter tier.\n32: - **`TESScraper._extract_from_json`** catches `AttributeError` in addition to `JSONDecodeError, KeyError, TypeError` — the `__NEXT_DATA__` JSON can have null-valued fields\n33: - **TESScraper URLs** come from `canonicalUrl` in Next.js JSON, which is a relative path; `src/scrapers/tes.py:108` prepends `https://www.tes.com` to make absolute URLs for Telegram links\n34: - **`scripts/setup_supabase.sql`** — required schema for the `job_listings` table; must be applied manually to Supabase before first run\n35: - Virtual environment at `.venv/` but dependencies are installed globally via home dir pip; `pip install -e .` not required\n36: - `src/notify/email_sender.py` was renamed from `email.py` to avoid shadowing stdlib `email` package\n37: - No lint, typecheck, formatter, or pre-commit config\n38: - **Tenacity retry** — every provider HTTP call wraps in `tenacity.Retrying` with `wait_random_exponential(multiplier=1, max=60)`; 3 attempts per model before rotating to next model or provider.\n39: - **`[PIPELINE]` logging** — every attempt logged as `[PIPELINE] Provider: groq | Model: ... | Result: Success/Fail | Attempt: N`. Parsable format for log aggregation.\n40: - **`validate_provider_configs()`** — startup validation with 2-minute deadline; probes all registered providers with a real scoring prompt. On 401/404 logs `[CONFIG_INVALID]` and removes provider from rotation. Does NOT consume `SCORER_PROVIDER`/`SCORER_FALLBACK` env vars.\n41: - **`ProviderRegistry` health state machine** — three-state health tracking: ACTIVE, COOLING_DOWN (300s canary after error), DEAD (3 consecutive cooldown failures). Dead providers stay removed for the session.\n42: - **Intra-provider model rotation** — each provider tries a primary → fallback chain internally before the cascade moves to the next provider. Groq: 1 model (from settings). NVIDIA: 2 models (primary + backup). OpenCode Zen: 2 models (`deepseek-v4-flash`, `deepseek-v4-pro`). OpenRouter/Gemini: 1 model each.\n43: - **Leaky-bucket pacing** — `batch_score()` splits work into chunks of `MAX_PER_CHUNK=5` with a `CHUNK_DELAY=20s` gap. Total pipeline ~3-4 minutes for 44 jobs.\n44: - **Provider weights** — `PROVIDER_WEIGHTS = {\"groq\": 40, \"nvidia\": 30, \"openrouter\": 20, \"opencode_zen\": 20, \"gemini\": 15}`. Higher weight = queried first. Does NOT correspond to RPM — just priority order.\n45: - **Cover letter `__LLM` / `__fallback` tagging** —