edup_store.py` — SQLite-backed `DedupStore` used as fallback when Supabase is unreachable; tables: `seen_urls`, `job_cache`\n64: - `src/storage/supabase_client.py` — all methods now fall through to `DedupStore` on `httpx.HTTPError`; `close()` cleans up SQLite\n65: - `src/notify/telegram.py` — includes `scoring_reasoning` in alert messages and cover letter captions\n66: - `src/generators/cover_letter.py` — has Groq (`_call_groq`) + `time.sleep(5)` in evaluation loop to avoid 429s; `_resolve_provider()` probes Groq → NVIDIA → OpenRouter → OpenCode Zen → Gemini\n67: - `src/main.py` — `run_pipeline()` handles Supabase failure gracefully, scores in-memory as fallback; `score_jobs_in_memory()` and `score_jobs_from_db()` use `batch_score()` for LLM calls\n68: - `tests/test_gemini_smoke.py` — smoke test for LLM provider resolution and score validity; run via `python3 tests/test_gemini_smoke.py`\n\n(End of file - total 68 lines)\n</content>",
