            "output": "=== TOUR ===\nStep 1: Project Overview\n  Description: Start here to understand what physics-job-hunter does. This document describes the full pipeline — scrape, deduplicate, upsert, score, notify — plus entrypoints, gotchas, and configuration. It's the single best onboarding resource.\n  Nodes: ['document:AGENTS.md']\n\nStep 2: Pipeline Entry Point & Orchestration\n  Description: main.py is the central orchestrator with the highest fan-out (22 edges) in the project. run_pipeline() chains all phases: scraping via run_scrapers(), deduplication via Supabase, scoring via score_jobs_in_memory/score_jobs_from_db, and notification via send_notifications(). The CLI entry point main() calls run_pipeline() and prints a summary.\n  Nodes: ['file:src/main.py', 'function:src/main.py:run_pipeline', 'function:src/main.py:main', 'function:src/main.py:run_scrapers', 'function:src/main.py:score_jobs_in_memory', 'function:src/main.py:score_jobs_from_db', 'function:src/main.py:send_notifications']\n\nStep 3: Configuration Foundation\n  Description: config.py is the highest fan-in module (8 incoming edges) — every downstream module imports it. The Settings class uses Pydantic BaseSettings to load all API keys, provider preferences, and notification config from .env. pyproject.toml defines CLI scripts and dependencies.\n  Nodes: ['file:src/config.py', 'class:src/config.py:Settings', 'config:.env', 'config:pyproject.toml']\n\nStep 4: Scraper Foundation & Abstract Base\n  Description: BaseScraper is the abstract base class for all scrapers, with the second-highest fan-in (7 inheriting classes). It provides shared HTTP client setup, BeautifulSoup4 parsing helpers, and URL utilities. All five scraper implementations inherit from it.\n  Nodes: ['file:src/scrapers/base.py', 'class:src/scrapers/base.py:BaseScraper']\n\nStep 5: Working Scraper: TES\n  Description: TESScraper is the primary working scraper, extracting job listings from TES.com. It first attempts to parse the Next.js __NEXT_DATA__ JSON embedded in the page, falling back to HTML parsing. It infers curriculum (IB, GCSE, etc.) from job details and constructs absolute URLs from relative canonicalUrl fields.\n  Nodes: ['file:src/scrapers/tes.py', 'class:src/scrapers/tes.py:TESScraper']\n\nStep 6: Additional Scrapers: Placeholder & Playwright-Based\n  Description: TeacherHorizonsScraper uses Playwright for Angular SPA rendering but is bypassed because detail pages require an activated teacher account. LinkedInScraper, SchroleScraper, and SearchAssociatesScraper are placeholders requiring login credentials — they log warnings and return empty lists. All implement the same scrape() interface from BaseScraper.\n  Nodes: ['file:src/scrapers/teacher_horizons.py', 'class:src/scrapers/teacher_horizons.py:TeacherHorizonsScraper', 'file:src/scrapers/linkedin.py', 'class:src/scrapers/linkedin.py:LinkedInScraper', 'file:src/scrapers/schrole.py', 'class:src/scrapers/schrole.py:SchroleScraper', 'file:src/scrapers/search_associates.py', 'class:src/scrapers/search_associates.py:SearchAssociatesScraper']\n\nStep 7: Scoring Engine: LLM & Rule-Based Fallback\n  Description: LLMScorer probes multiple LLM providers (opencode_zen, gemini, nvidia) at startup, caches the working provider, and scores jobs against the candidate profile. If all LLM providers fail, _score_via_rules applies keyword matching on title, curriculum, country, and salary with a base score of 30.\n  Nodes: ['file:src/scoring/llm_scorer.py', 'class:src/scoring/llm_scorer.py:LLMScorer', 'schema:data/profile.json']\n\nStep 8: Notifications: Telegram & Email\n  Description: send_telegram_alert sends formatted job alerts via the Telegram Bot API. email_sender.py provides dual-transport email digests via Resend API or direct SMTP with STARTTLS. Both are invoked by the orchestrator for jobs scored >= 80 and consume config for API keys.\n  Nodes: ['file:src/notify/telegram.py', 'function:src/notify/telegram.py:send_telegram_alert', 'file:src/notify/email_sender.py', 'function:src/notify/email_sender.py:send_email_digest', 'function:src/notify/email_sender.py:_build_digest_html', 'function:src/notify/email_sender.py:_send_via_resend', 'function:src/notify/email_sender.py:_send_via_smtp']\n\nStep 9: Database Storage & Schema\n  Description: SupabaseClient wraps CRUD operations on the job_listings table, used by the orchestrator for deduplication (skipping existing URLs) and upserting new jobs. The SQL migration creates the table with indexes on score, notified, source, and created_at for efficient querying. The setup script must be applied manually before first run.\n  Nodes: ['file:src/storage/supabase_client.py', 'class:src/storage/supabase_client.py:SupabaseClient', 'file:scripts/setup_supabase.sql', 'table:scripts/setup_supabase.sql:job_listings', 'table:scripts/setup_supabase.sql:idx_job_listings_score', 'table:scripts/setup_supabase.sql:idx_job_listings_notified', 'table:scripts/setup_supabase.sql:idx_job_listings_source', 'table:scripts/setup_supabase.sql:idx_job_listings_created']\n\nStep 10: Scheduler: Automated Daily Runs\n  Description: daily_run.py uses APScheduler to trigger run_pipeline() at configurable daily times (set via SCHEDULE_TIME in .env, e.g. 08:00,17:00,22:00). It imports both config.py and main.py, forming a tight cluster of 3 files with 3 internal edges. The scheduler runs as a background process, not as an OS cron job.\n  Nodes: ['file:src/scheduler/daily_run.py', 'function:src/scheduler/daily_run.py:start']\n\n",
