        "text": "@Alsini-physics-platform/agency-agents-main/ \n# 🎖️ System Orchestrator: Vertica l Slice Deployment\n\nExecuting the intelligence layer refactor. Below is the complete vertical slice for your Tiered Triage Engine, divided into the three precise integration phases we mapped out.\n\nThese blocks are designed to be dropped directly into your `src/scoring/llm_scorer.py` and `src/cover_letter.py` files.\n\n---\n\n### =========================================\n\n### PHASE 1: TIERED TRIAGE ROUTING (Backend Architect)\n\n### =========================================\n\nReplace your existing `score()` or evaluation loop in `llm_scorer.py` with this two-tier routing logic. It aggressively protects your NVIDIA API limits by making Groq the frontline bouncer.\n\n```python\nimport logging\nfrom typing import Dict, Any, Optional\n\nlog = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\ndef evaluate_job_tiered(self, job_text: str) -> Optional[Dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Tier 1 (Triage): Fast Groq filter. Drops anything < 60.\n    Tier 2 (Deep Eval): High-parameter NVIDIA analysis for top candidates.\n    \"\"\"\n    # 1. Triage Phase\n    triage_prompt = TRIAGE_SCORING_PROMPT.format(job_text=job_text)\n    \n    # Attempt Groq first (Fast/Cheap)\n    triage_result = self._call_provider(\"groq\", triage_prompt)\n    \n    # Fallback: If Groq hits a 429, NVIDIA assumes the triage role\n    if not triage_result:\n        log.warning(\"Groq triage unavailable (429/Timeout) — Escaping to NVIDIA for Tier 1.\")\n        triage_result = self._call_provider(\"nvidia\", triage_prompt)\n        \n    if not triage_result:\n        log.error(\"All triage providers failed.\")\n        return None\n\n    score = triage_result.get(\"score\", 0)\n\n    # 2. Threshold Gate\n    if score < 60:\n        log.info(f\"Triage Complete: Job discarded (Score: {score}).\")\n        return triage_result\n\n    # 3. Deep Evaluation Phase\n    log.info(f\"Triage Passed (Score: {score}) — Routing to NVIDIA for Deep Evaluation.\")\n    deep_eval_prompt = DEEP_EVAL_PROMPT.format(job_text=job_text)\n    \n    deep_result = self._call_provider(\"nvidia\", deep_eval_prompt)\n    \n    # Return deep result, or fallback to the triage score if NVIDIA fails mid-evaluation\n    return deep_result or triage_result\n\n```\n\n---\n\n### =========================================\n\n### PHASE 2: HARDENED LLM INSTRUCTIONS (Prompt Architect)\n\n### =========================================\n\nUpdate your prompt templates. These force deterministic formatting and explicitly ban the conversational \"hallucinations\" that break JSON parsers.\n\n**1. Deterministic Scoring Prompt (`TRIAGE_SCORING_PROMPT`)**\n\n```python\nTRIAGE_SCORING_PROMPT = \"\"\"\nYou are a strict, objective pedagogical evaluator. Evaluate the following job description for a Physics teaching position.\n\nCalculate a match score (0-100) based on these strict criteria:\n- Mandatory: Physics/Science curriculum alignment.\n- Mandatory: International or Secondary level focus.\n\nCRITICAL INSTRUCTIONS:\n- You must output ONLY a valid JSON object.\n- DO NOT output any introductory text, conversational filler, or markdown formatting (no ```json).\n- Your entire response must start with { and end with }.\n\nSCHEMA:\n{\n  \"score\": <integer 0-100>,\n  \"score_reasoning\": \"<Maximum 2 sentence justification>\"\n}\n\nJOB DESCRIPTION:\n{job_text}\n\"\"\"\n\n```\n\n**2. Tailored Cover Letter Generator (`COVER_LETTER_PROMPT`)**\n\n```python\nCOVER_LETTER_PROMPT = \"\"\"\nYou are a professional educational copywriter drafting a highly targeted cover letter.\n\nCANDIDATE: Mahmoud altaher Alsini, Mechanical Engineer & Secondary Physics Teacher (PGCEi in progress).\nJOB DESCRIPTION: {job_text}\n\nCRITICAL CONSTRAINTS (HARD FAIL IF VIOLATED):\n1. LENGTH CEILING: Maximum 250 words.\n2. NO CLICHES: Strictly ban generic filler phrases (e.g., \"In today's fast-paced educational landscape\", \"I am thrilled to apply\", \"I believe I am the perfect fit\").\n3. ANCHORING: You MUST extract exactly 2 unique facts about the school's curriculum, ethos, or specific needs from the job description and explicitly mention them to prove this is not a template.\n\nOutput the cover letter text directly. No prefaces, no signature block placeholders.\n\"\"\"\n\n```\n\n---\n\n### =========================================\n\n### PHASE 3: COMPONENT INTEGRATION (System Orchestrator)\n\n### =========================================\n\nInject these resilience utilities into your pipeline to prevent upstream model hallucinations from crashing your local system.\n\n**1. String-Aware JSON Extractor**\nPlace this helper in your parsing utility to defensively handle markdown leaks and trailing commas.\n\n```python\nimport re\nimport json\n\ndef _extract_json(text: str) -> Optional[Dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Defensively extracts JSON from LLM outputs, ignoring pre/post-scripts.\"\"\"\n    if not text:\n        return None\n\n    # Strip markdown wrappers if the LLM ignored instructions\n    text = re.sub(r\"^\nhttp://googleusercontent.com/immersive_entry_chip/0\n\n**2. Streaming Token Circuit Breaker**\nIf an LLM enters an infinite \"thinking\" loop, it will consume your budget and block the thread. Use `httpx` timeouts combined with a strict maximum token cutoff.\n\n```python\nimport httpx\n\ndef safe_llm_post(url: str, headers: dict, payload: dict, timeout_sec: int = 45):\n    \"\"\"\n    Executes a hardened POST request to an LLM provider.\n    Enforces strict read/write timeouts to break infinite generation loops.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Enforce a hard ceiling on the model's generation length\n    payload[\"max_tokens\"] = payload.get(\"max_tokens\", 800)\n    \n    timeout_config = httpx.Timeout(\n        connect=10.0, \n        read=timeout_sec,   # Circuit breaker: drops connection if model stalls\n        write=10.0, \n        pool=10.0\n    )\n    \n    try:\n        with httpx.Client(timeout=timeout_config) as client:\n 